{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared vectors for the touch / pen long press that opens a ContextMenu",
    "(CoreContextMenuContract.defaultLongPressDuration, defaultLongPressSlop and",
    "exceedsLongPressSlop).",
    "Read by coui_core (the constants, the slop predicate, and a reference reading of every",
    "press), coui_flutter (every press is replayed on the ContextMenu as real pointer events,",
    "so the framework's LongPressGestureRecognizer has to answer the table) and coui_web",
    "(every press is replayed on the ContextMenu's press tracker with a manual clock). A",
    "change on one platform fails the other.",
    "All coordinates are in logical px (Flutter) or CSS px (Web), relative to the top-left",
    "of the region that carries the menu. All times are ms since the first 'down'.",
    "drift: a pointer that went down at 'origin' and is now at 'point' - does it exceed the slop?",
    "presses: a list of pointer events, replayed in order, with the clock advanced to 'until'",
    "after the last one. 'opens' is where the menu ended up open (null when it did not) - at",
    "the point the pointer went DOWN, not where it drifted to. Events: down, move, up,",
    "cancel (the system took the pointer), and the Web-only scroll (the page or a scroller",
    "moved), contextmenu (the browser's own event) and touchend.",
    "'platforms' names who replays a press (absent: both). The Web-only presses cover what",
    "Flutter has no counterpart for: the browser may send its own contextmenu event for the",
    "same gesture ('claims' says, per contextmenu event, whether the press owns it - an owned",
    "event must not toggle the menu it just opened), and the release of a press that opened",
    "the menu is consumed so the click that may follow it does not reach the page",
    "('consumes', per touchend event). Instants are kept clear of the hold and of the Web's",
    "release window, so a tie between a timer and an event is never asked."
  ],
